{"id": "EUVD-2026-39208", "enisaUuid": "0bc83192-d92a-3f3a-bb8b-8251ffb79d0a", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: cfg80211: enforce HE/EHT cap/oper consistency\n\nXiang Mei reports that mac80211 could crash if eht_cap is set\nbut eht_oper isn't. Rather than fixing that for the individual\nuser(s), enforce that both HE/EHT have consistent elements.", "datePublished": "2026-06-25T08:39:47", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-15T10:07:44", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/afe815a67ec8f2fd03c261fb64f5cde7eb05c17a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0f5e9ddd7e8e7758771a63cdd498a2007dc8da7a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/cb9959ab5f99611d27a06586add84811fe8102dc"], "aliases": ["GHSA-gff8-2g4x-324x", "CVE-2026-53257"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.11, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "169ff65e-5a01-32b6-abdf-36814e5ebbbc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "22c64f37e1d4e757b0073a72f1439c2c3509c5cb <cb9959ab5f99611d27a06586add84811fe8102dc"}, {"id": "341f4ffc-d6e0-3126-9b63-8775f39ed406", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "22c64f37e1d4e757b0073a72f1439c2c3509c5cb <afe815a67ec8f2fd03c261fb64f5cde7eb05c17a"}, {"id": "37e032fc-d9f4-314f-9e03-bb16fca846a9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "42e0751c-7a28-3092-8974-0fe08f6af022", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1"}, {"id": "9416e874-6697-34b7-8108-e289adaa409a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "22c64f37e1d4e757b0073a72f1439c2c3509c5cb <0f5e9ddd7e8e7758771a63cdd498a2007dc8da7a"}, {"id": "a064d2b2-9833-3b54-8d5f-87cf5b4ec408", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.0.13"}, {"id": "e5118567-c934-389e-b8dc-8984f9eb3cb8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor":